\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  One wish have I, greater than all others;
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj fills my soul from morn' till night.
\par In this vale of tears I know no other
\par than keep heart and soul a right.\tab 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj Looking to the man who bled in anguish
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj Facing death, how long He had to languish!
\par Then His head sank to His breast;
\par Drank God's cup without protest.
\par 
\par \pard\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. He will always be to me the token
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1 of the silent Lamb of God.\cf0 
\par Tho' sore wounded, He no curse hath spoken,
\par tho' the path of death He trod.
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li180\sl190\slmult0\qj How He strove to gain my soul's salvation!
\par How His merit brought me consolation!
\par This assurance I received
\par  When He cried: it is achieved.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Jesus, may I ever be reminded
\par     of Thy grace and of my guilt.
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj  Plagued by sinfulness, in darkness blinded,
\par  With Thy patience me didst shield!
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj For the lost sheep He has longed and waited;
\par  Ever called the shepherd, unabated.
\par  Gave His precious blood as toil
\par  For the ransom of my soul.
\par 
\par \pard\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.  I am Thine, assure me with Thy Amen.
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   Blessed Jesus, Thou art mine!
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj   Let Thy precious name be seen by all men
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0   burnt within me, I am Thine!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li144\sl190\slmult0\qj With Thee do all things, all else forsaking;
\par   live in Thee, in death with Thee partaking;
\par   even in my final hour
\par \pard     pledge my life with all my pow'r.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

